WEBVTT

00:01.880 --> 00:05.780
<i>This world is filled with 
too many games to count,</i>

00:06.980 --> 00:11.080
<i>though the vast majority simply 
come and go in obscurity.</i>

00:12.580 --> 00:15.420
<i>The greatest of all games</i>

00:15.420 --> 00:20.690
<i>is the fully immersive VR game boasting 
over 30 million players worldwide—</i>

00:20.690 --> 00:25.340
<i></i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>, which rightly 
earns the title of "god-tier game"!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:30.940
<i>One lover of trash games, Rakuro Hizutome,</i>

00:30.940 --> 00:34.160
<i>is trying out the god-tier 
game, </i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i>

00:34.930 --> 00:39.640
<i>What adventures await him there?</i>

02:11.420 --> 02:16.490
Winner

02:11.420 --> 02:16.490
Kei Uomi

02:11.960 --> 02:17.460
<b>Errands, Cultivation, and Game Progress</b>

02:13.420 --> 02:15.790
<i>Okay, let's move on to fortunes.</i>

02:15.790 --> 02:18.200
<i>Number one star sign is...</i>

02:18.200 --> 02:21.120
<i>Gemini! You have the best luck today.</i>

02:21.120 --> 02:24.290
<i>Your lucky item is roller skates.</i>

02:24.290 --> 02:28.240
<i>Gosh, I wish I could ride 
roller skates to school!</i>

02:28.240 --> 02:32.970
<i>But where would I get some?</i>

02:29.440 --> 02:33.720
Gotta say, it's one well made game...

02:34.500 --> 02:36.720
<i>Shangri-La Frontier.</i>

02:40.100 --> 02:43.600
I'd originally meant it to 
just kill a little time.

02:43.430 --> 02:46.220
<b>Kei Uomi</b>

02:43.640 --> 02:46.220
<b>Pro Gamer
With "Nitro Squad"</b>

02:46.630 --> 02:47.730
But...

02:48.620 --> 02:54.860
Mwahaha

02:48.620 --> 02:54.860
Gwahaha

02:49.880 --> 02:54.370
The thought of them enjoying it 
without me really ticks me off!

02:55.270 --> 02:59.520
Still, there's just a week 
until the big tournament,

02:59.520 --> 03:02.050
so I'd better work out the last of the kinks.

03:06.650 --> 03:10.660
Check out Inventoria Key ASAP, man!

03:14.370 --> 03:15.650
Scratch that.

03:15.650 --> 03:19.820
I really can't bear to 
let them get ahead of me!

03:33.910 --> 03:34.900
Okay!

03:39.360 --> 03:40.990
<b>The Serpent's Apple</b>

03:39.600 --> 03:40.990
Did you see it?

03:40.990 --> 03:44.320
That awesome sci-fi armor lineup?!

03:44.710 --> 03:49.260
I could take on the entire 
<i>SLF</i> playerbase with that!

03:49.260 --> 03:50.600
Yeah, I saw it!

03:50.600 --> 03:53.840
If you could use that stuff, it'd change up
the whole game, for real!

03:53.840 --> 03:54.630
Yeah!

03:54.630 --> 03:56.600
So, what now? What now?!

03:56.600 --> 03:58.730
Well, about that...

04:00.570 --> 04:06.540
Before I came here, I went into the storage 
space and checked a few things out.

04:06.540 --> 04:07.680
And?!

04:08.410 --> 04:10.680
My conclusion is...

04:13.980 --> 04:17.770
At the moment, they're not useful 
as anything more than art pieces.

04:23.150 --> 04:25.930
Those tactical machines and power armors

04:25.930 --> 04:30.660
seem to require a power source called 
a "Non-Standard Ether Reactor,"

04:30.660 --> 04:33.660
Non-Standard Armament: Wire
Keep-Out Wire

04:30.660 --> 04:33.660
Non-Standard Armament: Blade 
Harbinger

04:30.660 --> 04:36.090
an item I've never heard of 
and have no idea where to get.

04:37.990 --> 04:43.170
And you can't use the weapons 
without the power armor on, so...

04:43.380 --> 04:44.820
No way!

04:44.820 --> 04:47.550
I got so excited, I didn't dig any deeper...

04:47.760 --> 04:51.600
Actually, I've got a 
Non-Standard Ether Reactor.

04:52.310 --> 04:53.060
Gross!

04:54.790 --> 04:56.730
Where the hell did you get that?!

04:56.730 --> 05:00.140
Maybe it's 'cause I did most 
of the fighting against Kirin,

05:00.140 --> 05:02.220
but I got it in my loot.

05:02.340 --> 05:03.570
<b>Non-Standard Ether Reactor</b>

05:03.570 --> 05:06.370
I underestimated you, Mr. Bondage Rodeo!

05:06.370 --> 05:09.420
Damn it! Wish I coulda seen that rodeo.

05:09.420 --> 05:11.830
It's my one regret of the Wethermon fight...

05:12.090 --> 05:16.080
It seems like it's damaged, though.

05:13.390 --> 05:16.080
<b>Non-Standard Ether Reactor</b>

05:13.390 --> 05:16.080
<b>Damaged</b>

05:16.080 --> 05:18.460
You can't fix it at a shop?

05:18.460 --> 05:22.150
The blacksmiths I went to all 
turned me away at the door.

05:22.150 --> 05:25.240
"I can't fix a thing if I've 
got no idea what it is."

05:25.240 --> 05:28.260
Yeah, being a Divinity-era relic and all...

05:28.520 --> 05:31.670
We might need a specialized blacksmith.

05:31.670 --> 05:33.630
Or a special item...

05:34.410 --> 05:36.020
Either way, I'm stumped.

05:38.170 --> 05:40.440
I might know a way to get it fixed.

05:42.130 --> 05:44.680
Hey! You did that on purpose!

05:45.530 --> 05:48.110
Hey, are you serious about that?

05:48.110 --> 05:50.160
Well, no guarantees.

05:50.160 --> 05:53.460
And since it involves a unique scenario, 
it might be hard to get you there.

05:54.060 --> 05:57.580
I was hoping you'd let me 
borrow that item of yours.

06:00.200 --> 06:01.510
Okay.

06:01.970 --> 06:04.120
Or so I'd like to say...

06:04.120 --> 06:05.490
But I've got a condition.

06:06.510 --> 06:10.800
I wanna know the unlock conditions for 
that unique scenario you're hiding.

06:12.530 --> 06:14.220
Come on, Katzo.

06:14.220 --> 06:17.650
I mean, it's not like I'm 
triggering my own unique stuff!

06:17.650 --> 06:20.620
I gotta piggyback on everyone else's stuff!

06:20.620 --> 06:23.250
You sulk about the most annoying things.

06:23.890 --> 06:27.770
<i>In </i>SLF<i>, information on uniques 
is extremely valuable.</i>

06:28.320 --> 06:31.240
<i>Even more so for those with monopolies on it.</i>

06:32.020 --> 06:36.250
<i>The three of us didn't come together 
purely out of a sense of camaraderie.</i>

06:36.940 --> 06:41.090
<i>To protect our own profits, 
we won't share information easily.</i>

06:41.090 --> 06:45.430
<i>And... the same goes for Katzo-kun.</i>

06:48.090 --> 06:50.930
It's not like it showed me the 
conditions when I unlocked it,

06:51.750 --> 06:54.490
so I can only explain my 
own situation at the time.

06:54.490 --> 06:55.600
Is that enough?

06:56.500 --> 06:57.510
You mean it?

06:57.510 --> 07:00.100
Don't act so shocked. 
You're the one who asked.

07:00.600 --> 07:02.690
I didn't wanna reveal this stuff,

07:02.690 --> 07:04.690
but you want a show of good faith, right?

07:05.140 --> 07:08.950
And like I just said, I don't have any 
proof that these are the conditions.

07:12.890 --> 07:16.080
All right, here I go.

07:17.170 --> 07:18.500
What I did was...

07:24.170 --> 07:28.530
<b>Unique Monster
Lycagon the Nightslayer
 Encountered</b>

07:24.680 --> 07:28.550
Unique monster, Lycagon the
Nightslayer, encountered.

07:28.940 --> 07:31.990
Unique... monster?

07:34.180 --> 07:35.800
At level 20 or less,

07:36.580 --> 07:39.120
I lasted five minutes without taking damage

07:39.120 --> 07:42.690
against the randomly encountered unique 
monster, Lycagon the Nightslayer,

07:43.050 --> 07:47.350
then landed around 200 critical 
hits with a vorpal weapon.

07:48.570 --> 07:50.490
You expect me to do that?!

07:50.490 --> 07:52.930
You acrobatic asshole!

07:53.690 --> 07:55.570
What are you mad at me for?!

07:55.570 --> 07:57.990
It's like if he asked you how you fly,

07:57.990 --> 08:01.110
and you told him to work out his pecs!

08:01.110 --> 08:05.170
You think there's no harm in telling me 
because there's no chance I'll do it, right?!

08:05.170 --> 08:06.710
Hey, this isn't fair!

08:06.710 --> 08:08.410
I gave you a genuine answer!

08:08.410 --> 08:09.790
Fine, whatever!

08:09.790 --> 08:11.880
Just take the stupid thing already.

08:11.880 --> 08:12.670
Hey!

08:12.930 --> 08:15.550
Oh, right. Sunraku-kun...

08:16.000 --> 08:16.930
What now?

08:17.190 --> 08:20.430
Could I get back that thing I left with you?

08:21.560 --> 08:22.880
What thing?

08:22.880 --> 08:25.350
Oh, right. Forgot I hadn't done that.

08:26.600 --> 08:28.300
Hey, Sunraku-kun.

08:29.960 --> 08:32.740
Could you hang onto this for a while?

08:34.230 --> 08:36.160
Um, sure.

08:36.890 --> 08:38.160
Item ownership has been transferred.

08:43.370 --> 08:45.640
<b>Reward Scales</b>

08:46.120 --> 08:49.570
That thing you were messing with 
in the Wethermon fight, right?

08:49.570 --> 08:51.040
You said you'd borrowed it, right?

08:51.650 --> 08:53.130
Item ownership has been transferred.

08:53.130 --> 08:57.350
From an NPC organization 
called the Golden Scales.

08:57.350 --> 09:02.390
I think it's part of one of the highest 
classes of items in all <i>Shangri-La Frontier</i>.

09:03.140 --> 09:04.860
Theoretically, if you throw in enough money,

09:04.860 --> 09:08.520
you can get stats even higher 
than those of a unique monster.

09:09.020 --> 09:12.170
You'd need the budget of a small 
country to do it, of course.

09:12.490 --> 09:15.930
It seems the Inventoria can't 
be removed once it's equipped,

09:15.930 --> 09:18.530
so I'd expected it to be sold off...

09:18.530 --> 09:20.460
What? Really?

09:20.460 --> 09:24.800
Right, they did mention it 
becoming a part of your body...

09:25.290 --> 09:30.290
Fortunately, it doesn't seem to have been 
taken, even as part of the PKK penalty.

09:30.660 --> 09:35.550
But this is the one thing I didn't 
want to lose, so I laundered it.

09:35.780 --> 09:37.110
Laundered it?

09:37.550 --> 09:41.310
A little trick to keep your items 
from being lost to the penalty.

09:41.870 --> 09:44.340
The penalty for PKing means 
that when you're killed,

09:44.340 --> 09:47.580
ownership of your items transfers 
to the person who killed you.

09:47.580 --> 09:52.330
And you have to pay a fee in proportion 
to your wrongdoing—your karma points.

09:53.090 --> 09:58.230
I think it sets your affection levels from 
most NPCs to the lowest level possible,

09:58.230 --> 09:59.580
too, but that's fine.

09:59.930 --> 10:02.830
The fee this time was pretty annoying.

10:03.290 --> 10:06.660
Oh, no!

10:06.660 --> 10:09.920
When you're killed, 
even items kept in storage will be

10:08.600 --> 10:10.230
Pencilgon's Storage

10:09.920 --> 10:14.380
automatically seized and sold off
to help pay off the fee.

10:11.350 --> 10:13.020
Sold Off

10:12.110 --> 10:14.480
Repayment

10:14.960 --> 10:18.970
Protecting certain items from this 
seizure is called "laundering."

10:19.210 --> 10:21.100
So instead of putting them in storage,

10:21.100 --> 10:24.510
you gave them to Sunraku 
before Psyger-0 killed you?

10:24.510 --> 10:26.240
You can actually do that?

10:26.240 --> 10:27.480
Seems like a pretty big exploit...

10:27.750 --> 10:30.660
No. Even if you hand over the item,

10:30.660 --> 10:33.230
it'll still search through 
your history and sell it off.

10:33.230 --> 10:34.230
Huh?

10:34.230 --> 10:36.890
Then why didn't the Scales go away?

10:38.110 --> 10:39.760
The Scales aren't really mine.

10:39.760 --> 10:44.320
Their ownership fundamentally 
lies with The Golden Scales.

10:45.130 --> 10:46.780
What matters here is that

10:46.780 --> 10:51.500
items you don't have ownership of 
won't be automatically sold off.

10:51.750 --> 10:56.180
But you can't transfer ownership just 
by handing an item to someone else.

10:56.510 --> 11:01.890
So when Psyger-0 killed me, 
even if I'd been carrying the Scales,

11:06.010 --> 11:09.470
their ownership by The Golden 
Scales wouldn't have changed.

11:09.470 --> 11:13.270
So they wouldn't have been sold off; 
they'd probably just be dropped as an object.

11:13.620 --> 11:17.530
I think I get the idea, 
but how's that laundering?

11:17.530 --> 11:21.120
Isn't it just the Scales falling 
outside the standard penalty purview?

11:22.300 --> 11:26.030
You can exploit that property to 
do some very interesting things.

11:26.990 --> 11:29.270
"The scales preserve the balance.

11:29.270 --> 11:32.290
Let the past be my payment, 
and return what has been offered."

11:38.550 --> 11:42.400
<b>Tome of Truth: The Tombguard</b>

11:38.550 --> 11:42.400
<b>Flower Pin of Bygone Prayers</b>

11:42.630 --> 11:46.170
That's the Tome of Truth and... 
What's the flower thing?

11:46.980 --> 11:49.370
My loot from the Wethermon fight.

11:49.690 --> 11:53.560
Looks like the three of us each 
got slightly different items.

11:53.560 --> 11:55.650
<b>Clear Sky Skillbook</b>

11:55.810 --> 11:59.390
Let's see... "Clear Sky Skillbook"?

11:57.070 --> 11:59.650
<b>Clear Sky Skillbook
</b>A digital record of sword techniques
left by a Divinity-era swordsmaster.

11:59.900 --> 12:06.780
I offered the Flower Pin of Bygone Prayers 
and the Tome of Truth to the Scales.

12:06.780 --> 12:11.400
In that instant, ownership of the 
Pin transferred to the Scales,

12:06.780 --> 12:12.270
<b>Ownership</b>

12:06.780 --> 12:12.270
<b>Offering</b>

12:11.400 --> 12:15.290
which meant they no longer 
had physical existence.

12:15.890 --> 12:19.490
So they couldn't be seized?

12:19.490 --> 12:20.220
Right.

12:20.220 --> 12:23.070
And it actually let you get 'em back?

12:23.070 --> 12:26.800
If you pay the price within one week, 
you can retrieve the items.

12:27.380 --> 12:30.810
Of course, I had to give up 
40 levels to make it happen...

12:32.330 --> 12:35.810
But if it means I get to keep this pin, 
I won't miss them.

12:39.320 --> 12:42.910
On top of that, in order 
to rent out these Scales,

12:42.910 --> 12:44.820
I used my main weapon as collateral!

12:45.110 --> 12:50.010
The Scales' power transferred its ownership 
to the organization, so it's also safe!

12:52.120 --> 12:55.710
So much for wiping the slate 
clean on your crimes...

12:55.710 --> 12:57.460
So, how much was the fee?

12:57.460 --> 12:59.180
A good 500 million mahni.

12:59.180 --> 13:00.250
You won't get it outta me.

13:00.250 --> 13:01.890
I don't need to borrow it.

13:01.890 --> 13:03.940
I can totally afford it.

13:04.380 --> 13:07.080
The most recent fight proved it to me.

13:07.080 --> 13:07.970
Proved what?

13:09.500 --> 13:11.980
Hunting unique monsters is 
a profitable enterprise.

13:13.950 --> 13:15.980
As simple as that, huh?

13:17.050 --> 13:20.230
On that point, I have a proposal.

13:22.200 --> 13:23.740
Would you two like...

13:25.070 --> 13:26.990
to form a clan with me?

13:46.550 --> 13:47.340
Rock...

13:47.340 --> 13:48.390
Paper...

13:48.390 --> 13:50.050
Scissors!

13:51.610 --> 13:54.020
Yeah! Pencilgon loses!

13:54.020 --> 13:57.490
That means Pencilgon's our clan leader!

13:57.490 --> 13:58.820
Oh, yeah!

14:00.020 --> 14:01.900
Best out of three!

14:01.900 --> 14:03.290
Nothing doing!

14:04.030 --> 14:08.600
I should've known I couldn't beat
their reaction speed...

14:08.600 --> 14:10.960
Just figuring that out, are you?!

14:08.600 --> 14:12.200
Smug

14:14.300 --> 14:17.490
I'm not cut out to be a 
leader... but ah, well.

14:17.490 --> 14:20.990
Okay, Leader!
Here's your first job.

14:21.360 --> 14:23.210
What should our clan name be?

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Unique Hunters</b>

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Outrage</b>

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Trash Game Alliance</b>

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Wolfgang</b>

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Gold Rush</b>

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Pike-Mounted Heads</b>

14:23.210 --> 14:25.960
<b>Pencilgon-chan
and Her Errandboys</b>

14:31.880 --> 14:32.600
Okay.

14:33.750 --> 14:36.480
What about this one, then?

14:36.480 --> 14:38.780
Sounds good to me. Pretty cool.

14:38.780 --> 14:43.060
I'd have been okay with 
"Pencilgon-chan and Her Errandboys," myself.

14:43.060 --> 14:45.010
I would not have.

14:43.090 --> 14:50.070
<b>Unique Hunters</b>

14:43.090 --> 14:50.070
<b>Outrage</b>

14:43.090 --> 14:50.070
<b>Trash Game Alliance</b>

14:43.090 --> 14:50.070
<b>Gold Rush</b>

14:43.090 --> 14:50.070
<b>Pike-Mounted Heads</b>

14:43.090 --> 14:50.070
<b>Pencilgon-chan
and Her Errandboys</b>

14:45.770 --> 14:47.230
All right, my fellows.

14:47.230 --> 14:49.640
Let's ready our drinks.

14:50.070 --> 14:53.960
We will henceforth become 
wolves venturing through the

14:53.960 --> 14:57.610
world of <i>Shangri-La Frontier </i>
in search of unique monsters—

14:58.080 --> 15:01.580
<b>Wolfgang</b>

14:58.080 --> 15:01.580
And in celebration of Clan 
Wolfgang's founding...

15:01.910 --> 15:03.940
A toast!

15:09.960 --> 15:13.120
So, what'll our emblem be?

15:13.120 --> 15:14.400
I think that one...

15:14.400 --> 15:15.500
should be up to Pencilgon!

15:15.500 --> 15:16.860
Get to it, Leader!

15:16.860 --> 15:19.100
Stop making me do everything!

15:20.150 --> 15:23.020
Didn't know there was a pub back here...

15:23.020 --> 15:25.050
I figure it can just be whatever.

15:25.050 --> 15:26.030
Same here.

15:26.030 --> 15:27.260
C'mon, man.

15:27.260 --> 15:29.650
If we're gonna make a guild, 
at least think stuff over!

15:30.280 --> 15:33.130
Wow, there's basically no one here.

15:33.660 --> 15:36.070
Hey, you guys.

15:36.070 --> 15:38.160
I've got a question for you.

15:38.950 --> 15:40.560
I've been searching for the trio

15:40.560 --> 15:44.170
who beat the unique monster 
from that recent announcement.

15:44.670 --> 15:46.030
Their names are

15:45.560 --> 15:48.000
<i>Arthur Pencilgon</i>

15:46.030 --> 15:48.000
Arthur Pencilgon,

15:48.000 --> 15:50.260
Oikatzo,

15:48.050 --> 15:50.260
<i>Oikatzo</i>

15:50.260 --> 15:52.550
and Sunraku...

15:50.300 --> 15:52.550
<i>Sunraku</i>

15:57.050 --> 16:00.380
Never heard of 'em!

16:00.380 --> 16:01.260
Hey!

16:01.260 --> 16:04.310
Hey, Leader! 
I thought you rented the place out!

16:04.310 --> 16:07.070
I don't recall ever saying that!

16:07.070 --> 16:10.070
I just said barely anyone ever went there!

16:10.370 --> 16:11.960
Well, it's good timing.

16:11.960 --> 16:13.770
Let's call the meeting to a close.

16:13.770 --> 16:16.540
My level dropped, 
thanks to the Evil Force and all,

16:16.540 --> 16:18.690
so I'd like to do some leveling, myself.

16:18.690 --> 16:23.580
Yeah, and I should turn in the 
Scales and get my main weapon back.

16:23.930 --> 16:26.650
You handle the reactor stuff, Sunraku-kun!

16:26.650 --> 16:27.590
You got it!

16:27.850 --> 16:29.960
And you figure out that emblem!

16:29.960 --> 16:31.140
Later!

16:31.970 --> 16:33.640
They split up!

16:33.640 --> 16:35.840
Hey, player named Sunraku!

16:35.840 --> 16:38.260
Wait! Don't run away!

16:38.260 --> 16:39.470
Terribly sorry!

16:39.470 --> 16:42.230
My name's not Sunraku! It's Samraku!

16:42.230 --> 16:43.730
You liar!

16:45.160 --> 16:46.630
Here we go!

16:49.630 --> 16:51.260
I'm back, Emul!

16:52.010 --> 16:53.250
Open a gate, would you?

16:56.510 --> 16:58.660
You're late, Sunraku-san!

16:58.660 --> 17:00.170
Positively tardy!

17:00.170 --> 17:03.490
Now, now. I'll explain later.

17:04.450 --> 17:05.420
Harrumph!

17:05.420 --> 17:08.380
Right, that creepy sword.

17:09.710 --> 17:12.520
I forgot to hand it back to Pencilgon.

17:13.030 --> 17:15.510
Well, next time.

17:15.510 --> 17:17.270
You chose the wrong escape route, buddy!

17:17.270 --> 17:19.510
You're heading right for a dead end!

17:19.840 --> 17:21.750
I just wanna ask you some questions.

17:21.750 --> 17:23.360
You don't have to run—

17:24.720 --> 17:26.800
Hey, he's gone.

17:29.590 --> 17:30.990
Where'd he go?

17:33.700 --> 17:36.560
Huh? Aniki Vash isn't here?

17:36.980 --> 17:42.210
I haven't seen Dadd—the boss 
since the day he spoke to you.

17:42.210 --> 17:43.560
Got it.

17:43.560 --> 17:46.250
So he's not necessarily 
always at the Palace, huh?

17:46.600 --> 17:51.280
I was hoping to go see him after I did my 
skill fusions and point distributions...

17:56.670 --> 18:00.060
You successfully learned 
your new skills, I see.

18:00.060 --> 18:02.200
Hey, bird-man...

18:02.510 --> 18:07.660
Would you like to peruse my skill grimoires?

18:07.660 --> 18:10.520
I'm kinda broke.

18:07.960 --> 18:10.520
<b>mahni</b>

18:10.520 --> 18:11.800
Hmph!

18:12.220 --> 18:14.120
<i>Don't "hmph" at me, lady.</i>

18:14.120 --> 18:16.970
<i>You were gonna rope me into a purchase 
the minute you saw a chance,</i>

18:16.970 --> 18:18.530
<i>you money-grubbing bunny.</i>

18:19.060 --> 18:21.530
Well, where shall we go next?

18:23.410 --> 18:27.540
Who else besides Aniki could 
fix the Ether Reactor?

18:29.370 --> 18:32.210
Probably not Bilac, but I might as well ask.

18:33.710 --> 18:35.670
Yeah, I can't fix that.

18:36.170 --> 18:37.670
Yeah, figured.

18:38.010 --> 18:42.410
Only an Ancient Craftsman can 
fix up stuff from the Divinity.

18:40.400 --> 18:42.410
<b>Ancient Craftsman</b>

18:42.790 --> 18:45.610
I'm only a Master Craftsman.

18:43.350 --> 18:45.370
<b>Master Craftsman</b>

18:46.060 --> 18:48.690
Pops is the only guy I know 
who could handle this.

18:48.910 --> 18:51.660
So you need the "Ancient Craftsman" job?

18:51.660 --> 18:52.820
Ah, well.

18:53.220 --> 18:57.240
I'll forget the reactor for now, 
and work on raising my fused skills.

18:58.630 --> 18:59.820
Raising?

19:00.450 --> 19:01.530
Growth?

19:03.600 --> 19:05.120
What is it?

19:05.120 --> 19:06.650
That's it!

19:06.650 --> 19:08.890
I just need to do some raising!

19:10.710 --> 19:12.940
If there's no Ancient Craftsman around,

19:12.940 --> 19:15.870
I just need to turn Bilac 
into an Ancient Craftsman!

19:17.080 --> 19:18.920
Don't underestimate the 
Ancient Craftsman title!

19:18.920 --> 19:21.380
It's not as easy as you make it sound!

19:21.380 --> 19:24.970
I'm not telling you to become a 
Divine Craftsman like Aniki Vash.

19:22.840 --> 19:28.270
<b>Divine Craftsman</b>

19:24.970 --> 19:28.270
Besides, it's a road you've 
got to go down someday, right?

19:29.180 --> 19:31.110
Which means now is the time!

19:31.110 --> 19:34.020
Let's make a try at that 
Ancient Craftsman title!

19:36.020 --> 19:37.640
Make a try?

19:38.390 --> 19:40.530
I'm not saying this out of a lack of faith.

19:40.530 --> 19:43.360
I'm saying it with full 
confidence in your skills!

19:43.360 --> 19:46.120
And I'll help you, of course!

19:46.120 --> 19:48.870
Big Sis Bee, I know you can do it!

19:52.740 --> 19:55.240
Me, an Ancient Craftsman?

20:00.430 --> 20:02.510
You got it, bird-man.

20:03.120 --> 20:04.900
I'll play along.

20:05.290 --> 20:07.510
I'm gonna become an Ancient Craftsman!

20:07.510 --> 20:10.520
Yay, Big Sis Bee!

20:10.520 --> 20:12.100
Hell yeah!

20:12.100 --> 20:15.190
Let's start the plan to cultivate Bilac!

20:15.190 --> 20:16.550
Yes, indeed!

20:16.550 --> 20:18.900
Y-Yeah!

21:49.990 --> 21:57.250
<b>SLF Mini</b>

21:50.770 --> 21:53.780
<i>SLF</i> Theater!

21:53.780 --> 21:57.250
<i><b>Making Oikatzo</b></i>

21:54.580 --> 21:56.010
Mini!

21:57.250 --> 23:31.340
<i><b>SLF Theater</b></i>

22:00.010 --> 22:02.090
That seems decent for my appearance.

22:02.580 --> 22:07.350
I get the feeling they'll tease me 
about the female avatar, though.

22:07.350 --> 22:09.640
Or maybe they'll totally ignore it?

22:09.640 --> 22:10.850
Okay, let's go with it.

22:10.850 --> 22:13.350
<b>Please input name.</b>

22:11.750 --> 22:13.350
Name...

22:13.960 --> 22:16.480
It's gotta have "Katzo" in there.

22:16.480 --> 22:19.160
Modor Katzo. Katzo Bushi.

22:16.640 --> 22:21.610
<b>Modor Katzo</b>

22:18.390 --> 22:21.610
<b>Katzo Bushi</b>

22:19.160 --> 22:21.610
After that should be...

22:24.570 --> 22:27.940
They've been playing <i>SLF</i> for a while.

22:27.940 --> 22:30.910
That means I'll be playing catch-up with 'em.

22:31.460 --> 22:33.830
Pursue. "Oi."

22:34.190 --> 22:35.410
Oikatzo, then.

22:35.410 --> 22:39.420
<b>Please input name.</b>

22:35.930 --> 22:39.420
<b>Oikatzo</b>

22:39.890 --> 22:41.530
Nice to meet you.

22:41.530 --> 22:44.330
Actually, that's not quite right...

22:44.810 --> 22:49.170
"Let's work hard together as Oikatzo," maybe.

22:49.870 --> 22:52.050
I guess I'll pick Monk as my job.

22:52.050 --> 22:53.900
And for origin...

22:55.450 --> 23:01.470
"If you play as a Wanderer, 
instead of starting in Firstia,

23:01.470 --> 23:05.820
you'll be dropped off somewhere in 
the first area, the Rampant Forest."

23:06.900 --> 23:09.950
What kind of weirdo would 
want to start off lost?

23:10.690 --> 23:12.450
Actually, I can imagine.

23:12.450 --> 23:14.330
I might even know someone like that...

23:17.540 --> 23:20.780
Okay, I'm getting a late start,

23:20.780 --> 23:22.830
but I'm gonna catch up in no time!

23:23.120 --> 23:26.750
Let's go, god-tier game, <i>Shangri-La Frontier<i>!</i></i>
